    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_BoardSettingsRow">Board settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_BoardHelp">The Board puts your games on cards you place yourself: any size and shape, each showing games from a source (Recently played, a collection, a saved filter…) or one pinned game. More games than cards: go past the edge for the next page. While editing: A on an empty square adds a card, A on a card picks it up (D-pad moves it, Y resizes), X opens its settings, Y removes it, B is done.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_BoardSourceHelp">Cards on the same source take turns: the next card shows the next game, and the next page carries on from there.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_BoardHiddenByFilter">{0} (hidden by Playnite's filter)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_TriArrange">Triangles point</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_ShapeTriangle">Triangle</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_TriAllUp">All pointing up</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_TriAllDown">All pointing down</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_TriTurns">Up, down, up… (they fit together)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_SecManual">MANUAL</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_ManualSettingsRow">Manual layout settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_ManualHelp">Manual: put tiles down yourself and choose the game (or widget, shortcut, logo…) for each. Edit: A on an empty square adds a tile, A on a tile picks it up (D-pad moves it, Y resizes), X its settings, Y removes it, B done. Widgets show only in the tiles you give them.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOC_KX_BoardHelp2">The Board puts your games on tiles you place yourself: any size and shape, each showing games from a list (Recently played, a collection, a saved filter…), a game you choose, a widget, a shortcut, or the highlighted game's logo or info. More games than tiles: go past the edge for the next page. Edit: A on an empty square adds a tile, A on a tile picks it up (D-pad moves it, Y resizes), X its settings, Y removes it, B done. Widgets show only in the tiles you give them.</sys:String>
